From 11ddab4d01cf90349662fee5963802364bb32e7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:34:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] agentHost: narrow the owned-directory match in the orphan
 sweep

The orphan sweep kept every directory whose name started with a known
session's key followed by a dash, so an unrelated orphan such as
keep-1-other next to a known keep-1 could never be reclaimed. A subagent
session's directory is <parent>/subagent/<toolCallId> after the data key
sanitises the slashes to dashes, so the sweep now derives that exact prefix
by passing buildSubagentSessionUriPrefix through the same key derivation the
producers use, and matches on it alone.

The chat channel rule had the same looseness: the base64url fragment of a
session URI is a prefix of the fragment of any session URI that extends it
on a three byte boundary, so a chat of copilot:/abcd was kept whenever
copilot:/abc was registered. A chat directory now has to end with the
fragment, or contain it followed by a dash as subagent chat directories do.
