From a484c066a2b7fafcd3273cd08386ba548e3e4c9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:44:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] agentHost: prune each stale external session
 independently

The prune loop awaited an unregister and then a data delete with no error
handling, so one failure abandoned every remaining stale row and skipped the
trailing list invalidation. Worse, the failing session had already lost its
registry row while its directory survived, which is exactly the unmatchable
orphan this prune exists to stop creating.

The data now goes first and the row second. A failed delete therefore leaves
the row intact, so the session is simply re-pruned on a later startup instead
of being orphaned, and the reverse case (data gone, row briefly kept) is a
state the listing already handles because a session whose database is absent
reads its metadata from the provider. Each session is wrapped so a failure is
logged and the loop continues, and the invalidation now runs whenever any
data was actually deleted rather than whenever any row looked stale.

Deleting before unregistering is safe for the will-delete subscribers: the
checkpoint and review services resolve their git refs from the event payload
and the session database, and neither consults the session registry.
